(8437, 267, 'What is a bibliography?', 'The list of sources used in a document', 'A backup file', 'A code library', 'A server list', 'A', 'A bibliography lists all referenced works.', 'BEGINNER', 1, 'MCQ', 1),
(8438, 267, 'What is a primary source?', 'Original research or first-hand evidence', 'A summary of research', 'A textbook summary', 'An encyclopedia', 'A', 'Primary sources present original findings.', 'BEGINNER', 1, 'MCQ', 1),
(8439, 267, 'What is a secondary source?', 'A work that discusses or summarizes primary sources', 'Original data', 'A raw dataset', 'First-hand evidence', 'A', 'Secondary sources interpret primary material.', 'BEGINNER', 1, 'MCQ', 1),
(8440, 267, 'What is the purpose of reviewing related work?', 'To understand existing solutions and avoid reinvention', 'To delete files', 'To format disks', 'To write code', 'A', 'Related work provides context and baseline solutions.', 'BEGINNER', 1, 'MCQ', 1),
(8441, 267, 'Which style is commonly used for citing research papers in computer science?', 'IEEE or ACM styles', 'Any style at random', 'No style', 'Only oral citations', 'A', 'IEEE and ACM are standard in computing research.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8442, 267, 'What does a systematic literature review emphasize?', 'A structured, repeatable search and selection process', 'Random reading', 'Quick summaries', 'Skipping sources', 'A', 'Systematic reviews follow a defined methodology.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8443, 267, 'How does a literature survey support the problem statement?', 'It shows the relevance and novelty of the problem', 'It writes the code', 'It deploys the system', 'It formats the disk', 'A', 'Prior work justifies the problem''s importance.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8444, 267, 'What is a research gap analysis used for?', 'Finding unaddressed aspects that the project can tackle', 'Deleting references', 'Formatting drives', 'Rebooting servers', 'A', 'Gap analysis targets opportunities for contribution.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8445, 267, 'Which of the following is a key part of a literature review?', 'Comparing and contrasting existing approaches', 'Only listing titles', 'Copying abstracts', 'Deleting sources', 'A', 'A good review synthesizes and critiques prior work.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8446, 267, 'What does ''state of the art'' refer to?', 'The most advanced current solutions', 'The oldest papers', 'Random code', 'Deleted research', 'A', 'State-of-the-art review covers the latest advances.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8447, 267, 'Which activity avoids self-plagiarism?', 'Citing your own prior work appropriately', 'Reusing text freely', 'Deleting references', 'Ignoring sources', 'A', 'Proper citation applies to your own previous publications too.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8448, 267, 'What is the role of a theoretical framework in a survey?', 'To organize the review around established theories', 'To delete data', 'To format disks', 'To write tests', 'A', 'Frameworks structure the analysis of literature.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8449, 267, 'What does evaluating source credibility involve?', 'Checking the author, publisher, and citations', 'Choosing the first result', 'Ignoring the source', 'Deleting the source', 'A', 'Credibility depends on authority and quality.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8450, 267, 'Which output summarizes the survey findings?', 'A literature review chapter or section', 'A compile log', 'A backup file', 'A sales report', 'A', 'The review documents the survey results.', 'INTERMEDIATE', 2, 'MCQ', 1),
(8451, 267, 'What is a meta-analysis?', 'Combining results from multiple studies statistically', 'A single case study', 'An opinion piece', 'A code review', 'A', 'Meta-analyses aggregate quantitative findings.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8452, 267, 'Which database is a major source of academic papers in computing?', 'IEEE Xplore or ACM Digital Library', 'A social media feed', 'A text file', 'A spreadsheet', 'A', 'IEEE Xplore and ACM DL index peer-reviewed computing research.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8453, 267, 'What is the difference between a reference and a citation?', 'A citation appears in text; a reference appears in the reference list', 'They are identical', 'References are oral', 'Citations are not needed', 'A', 'In-text citations map to full references at the end.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8454, 267, 'Why is it important to include very recent papers in a survey?', 'To reflect the current state of research', 'To fill pages', 'To delete older work', 'To avoid citations', 'A', 'Recent work ensures the review is current.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8455, 267, 'What is a bibliometric analysis?', 'Quantitative study of publication patterns and citations', 'A code review', 'A server scan', 'A budget audit', 'A', 'Bibliometrics analyze research output statistically.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8456, 267, 'How can a literature survey prevent duplicate research?', 'By revealing what has already been done', 'By deleting files', 'By formatting drives', 'By hiding references', 'A', 'Knowing prior work avoids reinventing solutions.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8457, 267, 'What is the purpose of a synthesis in a literature review?', 'To combine findings into new understanding', 'To list papers randomly', 'To delete sources', 'To format disks', 'A', 'Synthesis integrates prior findings meaningfully.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8458, 267, 'Which tool helps manage references efficiently?', 'Reference managers such as Zotero or Mendeley', 'A text editor', 'A media player', 'A calculator', 'A', 'Reference managers organize citations and bibliographies.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8459, 267, 'What does a critical appraisal of a paper assess?', 'The validity, methodology, and relevance of the study', 'The paper length', 'The font style', 'The file size', 'A', 'Critical appraisal judges research quality.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
(8460, 267, 'Which practice strengthens the credibility of a literature survey?', 'Documenting the search strategy and selection criteria', 'Deleting sources', 'Hiding methodology', 'Formatting drives', 'A', 'Transparent methods make reviews reproducible.', 'ADVANCED', 3, 'MCQ', 1),
